From 9cefc074ea06b30844162dfdc2f88a3e6e791423 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Langley <davidl@element.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:02:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Add an IndexedDB search index store for the web

`IndexeddbSearchStore` implements `SearchIndexFileStore`: the files of
each room's index, and values such as the reindex marker, in a
`<prefix>::search` database. The files are opaque, already encrypted
by the index when it is.

On the web, `ClientBuilder::search_index_store` and the FFI's
`with_search_index_store` take the path as the database prefix: the
client opens the store and the indexes are kept in memory and saved
through it, so the API is the same on every platform.
